<title>BRAZIL: TENNIS-BRAZIL TAKES 2-1 LEAD OVER AUSTRIA IN DAVIS CUP.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-BRAZIL TAKES 2-1 LEAD OVER AUSTRIA IN DAVIS CUP.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil took a 2-1 lead over</p>
<p>Austria in their Davis Cup World group qualifying tie on</p>
<p>Saturday when Brazil won the doubles after Austrian Thomas</p>
<p>Muster quit the match in the fifth set.</p>
<p>Result:</p>
<p>Jaime Oncins and Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) beat Thomas</p>
<p>Muster and Udo Plamberger (Austria) 7-6 4-6 6-3 3-6 2-0</p>
<p>retired</p>
</text>
